1 NOTE <p>About Harold E Adams</p><p>http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=3275977f-7dc5-4ee1-9947-ee029f222311&tid=4311400&pid=832920677</p>
1 NOTE <p>Id#: 0001057</p><p><p></p></p><p><p>Name: Adams, Harold E.</p></p><p><p></p></p><p><p>Date: Sep 15 1941</p></p><p><p></p></p><p><p>Source: Source unknown; Cleveland Necrology File, Reel #001.</p></
2 CONC p><p><p></p></p><p><p>Notes: Adams: Harold E., beloved husband of May, father of Celeste and Frank and the late Raymond and Delores, stepfather of Mildred, brother of Isolde Killian and Paul Gregory A
2 CONC dams, suddenly, Saturday evening, at his late residence, 1623 E. 33 st. Friends received at the home of the John I. Nunn Co., 2041 E. 89 st., after 4 p. m., Monday, Services Wednesday, Sept, 17, from 
2 CONC St. Columkille's Church at 9 a. m.</p><p><p></p></p><p></p>
1 NOTE <p>&nbsp;</p><p><p></p></p><p><p>    Harold was a swichman for the Nickel Plate Railroad. Working out of Collinwood, Ohio</p></p><p><p></p></p><p><p>    He also helped in the evacuation of school chil
2 CONC dren in Collinwood. There was a school fire</p></p><p><p></p></p><p><p>    and the doors opened the wrong way trapping  many chiidren.</p></p><p><p></p></p><p><p>    http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colli
2 CONC nwood_school_fire</p></p><p>    http://www.archive.org/stream/completestoryofc00neil#page/62/mode/2up</p>
