1 NOTE Mary Ann Cichon Cihon was born February 22, 1900 in Long Run, Ohio, according to her birth certificate.  Her first marriage was an arranged marriage, which was still commonplace at the time.  Her husb
2 CONC and was Tony Dragos (June 1894 - April 5, 1950) whose mother was Agnes Regiec.  Apparently, the two were related as distant cousins. Mary was largely unhappy in the marriage, which occurred in her mid
2 CONC dle teens. In a photograph dated “Summer of 1916,” she is already wearing a wedding band.  Mary secretly ran away and married another distant cousin, Michael Anthony Cihon, on his 18th birthday (A
2 CONC pril 7, 1927) in Milwaukee, WI in a civil ceremony.  Exactly when she divorced Tony Dragos is not clear.  Having married a man with the same last name, which was spelled without the extra 'C', would f
2 CONC orever cause confusion.  Michael Cihon, too, was a coal miner.  Mike and Mary were married in Sacred Heart Catholic Church in New Philadelphia, Ohio in 1957, celebrating their 30th wedding anniversary
2 CONC .  Mike died of a heart attack on October 12, 1974 at the age of 65.  Mary then moved to Cleveland to be closer to her daughter, Dolores.  On April 9, 1983, Mary suffered a massive stroke, from which 
2 CONC she did not recover.  One month later on May 8, (Mothers Day) Mary died of pneumonia in Euclid General Hospital.  She was 83.  Mike and Mary are buried in Northern Cemetery, Smithfield, Ohio.
