2 CONC p> <p>Carl J. Cihon Sr., 83, of Piney Fork, Ohio, passed away Friday, May 20, 2005, in the Kindred Hospital in Pittsburgh. </p> <p></p> <p>Carl was born Jan 25, 1922, in Piney Fork, a son of the late 
2 CONC Andrew and Mary Dragos Cichon.</p> <p>Carl was retired from the Consol Coal Co. and was a meat cutter for the Co-Op Stores for many years. He was a member of St. Therese Catholic Church in Piney Fork,
2 CONC  the Piney Fork American Legion Post #735, the Pine Valley Sportsman's Club and the AARP. Carl was a U.S. Navy veteran of World War II. <p></p> <p>In addition to his parents, Carl was preceded in deat
2 CONC h by two sisters, Clara Jablonski and Wanda Smith.</p> <p></p> <p>Surviving are his wife, Mary Truini Cihon, whom he married Nov. 9, 1946; one son, Carl J. (Debi) Cihon Jr. of Smithfield; two daughter
2 CONC s, Pam (Keith) Berry of Dillonvale and Maria (Brian) Parteli of Rayland; 11 grandchildren; seven great- grandchildren; two sisters, Toni Baumgartner of Oregon, Ohio, and Mary Agnes (Richard) Francisco
2 CONC  of Las Vegas, Nev.; and three brothers, Walter Cichon of Dillonvale, Henry (Evelyn) Cichon of Adena and Robert (Theresa) Cichon of Piney Fork. <p></p> <p>Friends and family may call at the J.E. Foste
2 CONC r Funeral Homes Inc., 107 Hill St., Smithfield, Saturday from 6 to 9 p.m. and Sunday from 2 to 4 and 7 to 9 p.m. Monday, friends and family may call at the St. Therese Church in Piney Fork from 10 a.m
2 CONC . until the time of the funeral liturgy with Mass at 11 a.m. Father Timothy Kozak will be the celebrant. Burial will follow in Holly Memorial Gardens. A vigil service will be conducted Saturday at 3:3
2 CONC 0 p.m. Full military graveside honors will be conducted by the Piney Fork American Legion Post #735. <p></p> <p>In lieu of flowers, donations may be made to the Piney Fork American Legion Post #735, c
