1 NOTE Dillonvale, St. Adalbert <p></p> <p>Founded: 1895; Renovated: 1973</p> <p></p> <p>In 1890, the Polish people organized the Benevolent Society of St. Joseph. They wanted a church, a parish. They provid
2 CONC ed themselves with three lots and a small dwelling place. They advertised in the newspapers for a priest, which they received in the form of Father Adalbert Dynia, a priest from Texas, who arrived in 
2 CONC 1895. He built a church, but left after serving one-and-a-half years. Father C. Tomaszewski of Pittsburgh, Pa. came occasionally to give the people services. In 1898, Father A. Swierczynski was appoin
2 CONC ted the first permanent pastor. <p></p> <p></p>
