1 NOTE <p>CICHON, Walter E. <p>March 8, 2012</p> <p>Times Leader</p> <p>Save </p> Bookmark and Share</p> <p></p> <p>CICHON, Walter E., 86, of Dillonvale, died Wednesday, March 7, 2012 at Liza's Place Wheelin
2 CONC g. He was born on February 16, 1926 in Piney Fork, a son of the late Andrew and Mary (Dragos) Cichon.</p> <p></p> <p>Walter was a life long member of St. Adalbert's Catholic Church and a recipient of 
2 CONC the Fidelis Award. He was a Veteran of the US Army and served in WW II, a 65 year member of the Fraternal Order of Eagles Aerie 1572, and the former American Legion Post 153 YTR. <p></p> <p>In additio
2 CONC n to his parents, he was preceded in death by his loving wife, Lottie (Boroski) Cichon in 1997, a brother, Carl Cihon, two sisters, Clara Jablonski, and Wanda Smith.</p> <p></p> <p>He was retired from
2 CONC  Consolidated Coal Co. after 42 years, and was the owner and operator of Vicki's Tavern for 35 years.</p> <p></p> <p>Surviving are his children, Richard S. (Marsha) Cichon Sr. of Rayland, Victoria M. 
2 CONC (Don) Kujawa of Narragansett, RI., Cheryl A. (William) Morelli of Glen Robbins, and Patricia C. Novak of Orient, Ohio. Grandchildren, Kimberly A. (Dan) Cermak of Dillonvale, Richard S. Cichon Jr. of M
2 CONC t. Gilead, Ohio, Mary Elizabeth (J.D.) Bruno of Rayland, and Don Vincent Kujawa of Narragansett, RI., great-grandchildren, Anna and Daniel Cermak and Jaxson Bruno. Two sisters, Toni Baumgartner of Ore
2 CONC gon, Ohio, and Mary Agnes (Richard) Francisco of Las Vegas, NV., two Brothers Henry (Evelyn) Cichon of Adena, and Robert (Theresa) Cichon 0f Piney Fork. <p></p> <p>Friends will be received at Wilson F
2 CONC uneral Home 154 Second Street Dillonvale on Friday March 9, 2012 from 2-8 p.m, with vigil services recited Friday at 5 p.m. at the Funeral Home. Funeral Liturgy with Mass will be celebrated on Saturda
2 CONC y at 10 a.m. at St. Adalbert's Church with Msgr. John C. Kolesar as celebrant. Burial follows in Holly Memorial Gardens Pleasant Grove. Full Military Graveside Honors will be conducted by the Dillonva
2 CONC le American Legion. <p></p> <p>To leave a condolence please visit www.wilsonfuneralhomes.com</p>
