1 NOTE <p>Helen Cichon Miller was born March 2, 1922. Helen was 25 1/2 years younger than her brother Andrew! While such age differences are fairly common today with remarriages, this age difference was with
2 CONC  the same parentage. (If it is assumed that Mary Jennie Regiec Cichon was born in 1875, she had three children &ndash; Josephine, Joann, and Helen -- all born AFTER the age of 40!) Helen worked in the
2 CONC  Hanna Coal Company Store after graduating Smithfield High School. On June 29, 1944, she married Stanley W. Miller of Dillonvale, who was stationed in Europe during World War II. The couple had one ch
2 CONC ild, Ronny, born in 1947. Helen was hospitalized for several months in 1953, due to Tuberculosis. In 1955, the Millers moved to 895 East 239th Street, across the street from John and Jennie Cichon, wh
2 CONC o lived at 884! They remained neighbors for three years, until John moved into a newly built home in Richmond Heights. Helen was diagnosed with kidney cancer in September 1980. She died on June 27, 19
2 CONC 81 at the age of 59. Stan remained in their Euclid home, frequently making visits to see his son, daughter-in-law, and his grandchildren, first in San Jose, CA, and later in San Antonio, TX. After a b
2 CONC rief illness, Stan died on April 18, 1994. He was 79 years old.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Let me begin with details on Grandma's father and mother, Joseph Cichon and Mary Regiec
2 CONC  (pronounced "Raggets"). We have only one B&amp;W photo of Joe and Mary, with their son, Frank, standing beside them. Joe had a handlebar mustache.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p>
