2 CONC lign: justify; background-position: 0px 0px;">Obituary for Richard Michael Cihon</h2> <div class="obituary-text" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-fam
2 CONC ily: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-stretch: inherit; line-height: 22px; vertical-align: baseline; outline: 0px; width: auto; height: auto; float: none; position: static; clear: n
2 CONC one; color: #404040; display: inline; text-align: justify; background-position: 0px 0px;"> <div class="obituary-text edit" style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-variant-caps: inherit; fo
2 CONC nt-stretch: inherit; line-height: 22px; vertical-align: baseline; outline: 0px; width: auto; height: auto; float: none; position: static; clear: none; display: inline; background-position: 0px 0px;" d
2 CONC ata-server-action="/obituaries/Richard-Cihon/ProcessUpdateTributeObituary" data-editclass="edit-obituary" data-fieldtype="textarea">Richard Michael Cihon, 82, of Kimbolton, passed away Monday, June 3,
2 CONC  2019 at the Cleveland Clinic. He was born November 27, 1936 in Piney Fork to the late Michael Anthony and Mary Ann (Cichon) Cihon. He was a graduate of St. Joseph's of Dover. He was a Korean War Navy
2 CONC  veteran. He was an Electronic Engineer for National Cash Register for 14 years and retired from his own business, RMC Enterprises in 2014. He was a member of St. Francis De Sales Catholic Church wher
2 CONC e he was the organist for years. On January 31, 1959, he married Lorla (Walter) Cihon who survives. He is also survived by his children, Richelle (Larry) Booth of Nolanville, TX, Dr. Irene (Dr. Jeff) 
2 CONC Dietz of Shaker Heights, Rose (Michael) Warren of Charlottesville, VA, Charles (Amy) Cihon of Bexley, and Mary (Hun) Yi of Delaware; 13 grandchildren; three great-grandchildren; and one on the way. He
2 CONC  was preceded in death by his son, Michael Cihon; four sisters, Irene Cihon, Evelyn Adams, Delores Srebott, and Rosemarie Sadar; one brother, Chester Cihon. Services will be Tuesday, June 18, 2019 at 
2 CONC 11 a.m. at St. Francis DeSales Catholic Church in Newcomerstown with Father Victor R. Wesolowski officiating. Visitation will be Monday, June 17, 2019 from 2 to 4 and 6 to 8 p.m. at Addy Funeral Home,
2 CONC  Newcomerstown.</div> &nbsp;</div>
