2 CONC hts Reserved </p><p> Questions? Contact us </p><p> Search obituaries nationwide</p> <p>JOSEPH SADAR </p> Visit Guest Book</p> <p>SADAR JOSEPH SADAR, 84, of Highland Heights, passed</p> <p>away Monday,
2 CONC  Feb. 20, 2012 at Manor Care in Willoughby.</p> <p>Born September 27, 1927 in Winbur, PA. He was a proud</p> <p>member of the S.N.P.J. Lodge #53. He served in the U.S.</p> <p>Army. He was the beloved 
2 CONC husband of the late Rose Marie</p> <p>Cihon Sadar; loving father of Timothy J. Sadar and Melanie</p> <p>Rose Aprahamian; grandfather of Lindsey, Colin, and Lauren;</p> <p>brother of John Sadar and Mar
2 CONC ie Sadar Bednar. He was</p> <p>preceded in death by his sons Joseph David and James J. Sadar; parents,</p> <p>Amelia and Frank Sadar Sr.; brother, Frank Sadar Jr. Funeral Mass will be</p> <p>Thursday,
2 CONC  Feb. 23, 2012 at St. Paschal Baylon, 5384 Wilson Mills Rd.,</p> <p>Highland Heights. THE FAMILY WILL RECEIVE FRIENDS FROM 5 TO 8</p> <p>P.M. WEDNESDAY, FEB. 22, 2012, at the DAVIS-BABCOCK FUNERAL</p>
2 CONC  <p>HOME, 4154 CLARK AVE., WILLOUGHBY. Burial will be at All Souls</p> <p>Cemetery in Chardon. Arrangements entrusted to THE KEVIN COYNE</p> <p>FUNERAL & CREMATION SERVICE. Online condolences at:</p> 
2 CONC <p>www.kevincoynefuneralservice.com</p> <p>Guest Book</p>
