1 NOTE <p>KANOSKI, Herman <p>February 19, 2012</p> <p>Times Leader</p> <p>Save </p> Bookmark and Share</p> <p></p> <p>KANOSKI, Herman, age 92, beloved Dad and Jagee, of Adena, Ohio, died Thursday February 16
2 CONC , 2012, at Autumn Health, of Adena, Ohio.</p> <p></p> <p>He was born April 19, 1919, in Adena, Ohio, son of the late Antoni "Tony" and Aniela Kowalczyk Kanoski.</p> <p></p> <p>He was the retired co-ow
2 CONC ner and operator of Kanoski Brothers Grocery Store in Adena, and a member of St. Casmir's Catholic Church, in Adena, Ohio. He enjoyed spending time with his family, cooking and gardening. <p></p> <p>I
2 CONC n addition to his parents he was preceded in death by his wife, JoAnn V. Cichon Kanoski (2002); four brothers, John, Felix, Walter, and Theodore Kanoski; and four sisters, Julia Figurski, Sophie Figur
2 CONC ski, Lottie Modolo, and Genevieve Andrzczyk. <p></p> <p>He is survived by a son, Michael (Lyn) Kanoski of Dillonvale, Ohio; daughter, Karen (Joseph) Gretchen of Adena, Ohio; sister, Helen Sobleski of 
2 CONC Adena, Ohio; four grandchildren, Kimberly (Jeff) Miller, Kris (Teresa) George, Michael (Misty) Kanoski, and Tracy ( Danny) Gonze; and nine great-grandchildren. <p></p> <p>Friends will be received to p
2 CONC ay tribute to Herman and celebrate his life Sunday from 2-6 p.m. at the Borkoski Funeral Home, Adena.</p> <p></p> <p>A Mass of Christian Burial Service will be celebrated Monday at 11 a.m. at St. Casm
2 CONC ir's Catholic Church, Adena, Ohio with Msgr. John Kolesar the celebrant.</p> <p></p> <p>Burial will be in Olive Branch Cemetery, Harrisville, Ohio.</p> <p></p> <p>Wake service Sunday 6 p.m. at the fun
2 CONC eral home.</p> <p></p>
