1 NOTE Angeline Cichon <p>CICHON, Angeline R. "Nellie," 96, of Piney Fork, Ohio, passed away</p> <p>Tuesday, April 5, 2011 at the Autum Health Care Inc., Nursing</p> <p>Home in Harrisville, Ohio.</p> <p>Nell
2 CONC ie was born in Piney Fork, Ohio on January 16, 1915, daughter</p> <p>of the late Joseph and Anna (Kryzsko) Jancura.</p> <p>She was a homemaker and was a member of St. Adalbert Catholic</p> <p>Church i
2 CONC n Dillonvale.</p> <p>In addition to her parents, Nellie was preceded in death by her</p> <p>husband, Steven T. Cichon in 1992; two sisters, Rose Korwek and</p> <p>Julia Kournoian; two brothers, Frank 
2 CONC and Joseph Jancura; an infant</p> <p>sister, Louise and a step-sister, Mary Krulcik.</p> <p>Surviving are her three sons, Steven E. (Martha) of Sarasota, Fla.,</p> <p>Louis J. (Linda) of Pataskala, Oh
2 CONC io, and James (Dolly) of Mt.</p> <p>Pleasant, Ohio; one sister, Anna Paolucci of Mich.; one brother,</p> <p>Walter (Georgianna) Jancura Sr. of Dillonvale, Ohio; brother-inlaw,</p> <p>Art Kournoian of 
2 CONC Mich. She is also survived by eight</p> <p>grandchildren, six great-grandchildren and one great-greatgrandson.</p> <p>Visitation will be on Friday 2-4 and 6-8 p.m. at the J.E. Foster</p> <p>Funeral Ho
2 CONC me, Inc., 107 Hill St. Smithfield, OH.</p> <p>Funeral Liturgy with Mass will be held on Saturday at 10 a.m. at</p> <p>St. Adalbert Church in Dillonvale, Ohio, with a visitation there from</p> <p>9:15 
2 CONC a.m. until time of the Mass at 10 a.m. Everyone will meet at</p> <p>the church. Msgr. John Kolesar will Celebrate the Mass and burial</p> <p>will follow in Northern Cemetery in Smithfield.</p> <p>Vigi
2 CONC l Service will be held at 3:30 p.m. Friday at the Funeral Home.</p> <p>www.jefosterfh.com</p>
