1 NOTE Biography <p>Helen A. Cihon Longshore Nielson, 84, a long time resident of Tucson, Arizona and formerly of Nemacolin, Pa., died on Wednesday, December 24, 2008 in Tucson. She was born July 30, 1924 in
2 CONC  Roswell, Ohio, a daughter of the late Joseph and Caroline (Antoletz) Cihon. Helen was a life long teacher and taught in schools in Ohio and Pennsylvania. Her longest teaching assignment was in Monroe
2 CONC ville, Pa. Helen moved to Tucson and taught at Los Ninos Elementary School, Sunnyside District. She resided in Mountain View Retirement Village for the past several years.  <p></p> <p>She is survived 
2 CONC by her husband, Corwin Nielson with whom she happily shared the last few years of her life; a brother, Dr. William P. Cihon of Tucson; a sister, Cecelia Yoskovich and her husband, Martin of Masontown,
2 CONC  Pa.; a niece, Suzanne Fish and her husband, Bill of Tucson; two sisters-in-law, Josephine (Jay) Cihon of Gates Mills, Ohio and Isabel Cihon of Mentor, Ohio and numerous nieces and nephews residing in
2 CONC  Pennsylvania and Ohio.  <p></p> <p>Deceased are four brothers, Adam Cihon, who died in infancy, Joseph Cihon, John Cihon and Steve Cihon and three sisters, Anna Cihon, who died in childhood, Margaret
2 CONC  (Marge) Mrazek and Mary Hurtuk. </p> <p></p> <p>A memorial service was held at 10:00 A. M. on Tuesday, December 30, 2008 in Adair Funeral Homes, Avalon Chapel, 8090 North Northern Avenue, Tucson, Ari
2 CONC zona. The family suggested that memorial donations to the American Lung Association of Arizona, 2819 E. Broadway Blvd., Tucson, AZ 85716. <p></p> <p>Facts</p> <p>Born: July 30, 1924</p> <p>Place of Bi
2 CONC rth: Roswell, Ohio</p> <p>Death: December 24, 2008</p> <p>Place of Death: Tucson, Ariz.</p> <p></p> <p></p> <p></p>
