1 NOTE <p>Mary K. Cihon <p>December 31, 2011</p> <p>The Herald-Star</p> <p>Save </p><p> Post a comment </p>  </p> <p>CIHON, Mary K. (Truini), 88, of Piney Fork, Ohio, passed away Friday, Dec. 30, 2011, at he
2 CONC r home.</p> <p></p> <p>Mary was born on Oct. 31, 1923, in Monongahela, Pa., daughter of the late Louis V. and Nicolina C. (Vita) Truini.</p> <p></p> <p>Mary was a former member of St. Theresa Catholic
2 CONC  Church in Piney Fork, and a current member of St. Adalbert Catholic Church in Dillonvale. She was a very active member of St. Theresa's Catholic Women's Club. Mary was a housewife and a loving grandm
2 CONC other and Noni. She was an avid Cleveland Indians fan, loved playing cards and working puzzles and she loved to grow African violets and orchids. <p></p> <p>In addition to her parents, Mary was preced
2 CONC ed in death by her husband, Carl J. Cihon Sr. who passed in 2005; brothers Sam, Joseph and Mario Truini.</p> <p></p> <p>Mary is survived by her children, son Carl J., Jr. (Debi) Cihon of Smithfield, O
2 CONC hio, daughter Pam (Keith) Berry of Dillonvale, Ohio, daughter Maria (Brian) Parteli of Smithfield, Ohio; her sisters, Jean Bednarski of Lincoln Park, Mich., and Amelia (Paul) Ferda of South Gate, Mich
2 CONC . Mary is also survived by her 11 grandchildren and 16 great-grandchildren, and one great-great-grandchild along with numerous relatives. <p></p> <p>Visitation for Mary will be held Sunday, Jan. 1, 20
2 CONC 12, from 2-4 and 6-8 p.m. at J.E. Foster Funeral Home in Smithfield, Ohio. Funeral Liturgy with Mass will be held for Mary on Monday, Jan. 2, at 10 a.m. at St. Adalbert Catholic Church in Dillonvale w
2 CONC ith Msgr. John Kolesar as Celebrant. Additional visitation will take place at the church from 9:15 a.m. until time of Mass. Everyone will meet at the church. Burial will follow in Holly Memorial Garde
2 CONC ns in Colerain, Ohio. Wake service is Sunday at 7:30 p.m. Memorial contributions may be made in Mary's memory to Piney Fork American Legion Auxiliary, St. Adalbert Catholic Church or Valley Hospice In
2 CONC c. Condolences may be made online at www.jefosterfh.com.
