2 CONC ="color1">8466 Mentor Ave.<br />Mentor, Ohio 44060</p> <p><p class="color2">(800) 228-4195<br />~ <br />(440) 255-3401</p></p> <p></div> </div> <div class="mainContent clearfix right"> <div class="obi
2 CONC ts_detail"> <div class="backLink"><a href="http://www.brunners.com/obituaries.php">&laquo; Back to Obituaries Listings </a></div><h2 class="brown">Robert J. ""Bob"" Metelko</h2> <img src="http://www.b
2 CONC runners.com/obits_images/metelko.jpg" alt="" /> <p><span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: small;"><span style="font-size: small;">Robert "Bob" J. Metelko, age 88, a 50 year M
2 CONC entor resident, passed away Thursday, July 18, 2013, at Emeritus in San Dimas, San Dimas, Calif. He was born Nov. 23, 1924, in Cleveland.</span></span></p> <p><span style="font-family: arial,helvetica
2 CONC ,sans-serif; font-size: small;"><span style="font-size: small;">Bob was a car dealership owner and car salesman in the local area for 38 years. He was a graduate of Collinwood High School, class of 19
2 CONC 43 and attended John Carroll University. He served in the U.S. Naval Service during </span><span style="font-size: small;">World War II</span><span style="font-size: small;">from 1943 to 1946 as an av
2 CONC iation radioman on the Avenger Night Torpedo Squad on the U.S.S. Independence in the Asiatic-Pacific conflict.&nbsp; Bob enjoyed life with friends and especially family and always had a positive attit
2 CONC ude, great sense of humor, and a caring personality. He was an avid golfer loved to go to casino's and loved to watch sports on T.V.</span></span></p> <p><span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans
2 CONC -serif; font-size: small;"><span style="font-size: small;">Survivors include his sons Gary (Maureen) Metelko of Mentor and Scott (Sheila) Metelko of Kirtland; granddaughters, Caitlin (Fiance, Corey Ku
2 CONC rilko) Metelko, Shannon and Brittany Metelko; his 20 year companion, Marjorie Arbaugh; and several nieces and nephews.&nbsp; Preceding Bob in death is his wife, Theresa (Cichon) Metelko; parents, Jose
2 CONC ph and Julia Metelko; and brothers, Ray and Rudy Metelko.</span></span></p> <p><span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: small;"><span style="font-size: small;">The family will 
2 CONC receive friends from 3 to 4:30 p.m. Sunday, August 25. The service will follow at 4:30 p.m. at Brunner Sanden Deitrick Funeral Home &amp; Cremation Center 8466 Mentor Ave., Mentor, OH. 44060. A recept
2 CONC ion and celebration of Bob's life will follow from 5 to 7 pm in the Reception Center on the Brunner Campus.</span></span></p> <p><span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: small;
2 CONC "><span style="font-size: small;">A private burial will take place at All Souls Cemetery, Chardon.&nbsp; Contributions may be made to The Lake County Ohio Veterans, 105 Main St. Painesville, OH. 44077
2 CONC  or Charter Hospice, 1012 East Cooley Drive, Suite G, Coulton, CA. 92324 or a </span><a href="http://media2.legacy.com/adlink/5306/1523365/0/3380/AdId=1862389;BnId=1;itime=264914092;ku=1349329;key=COY
2 CONC CADA;nodecode=yes;link=http://www.legacy.com/obituaries/news-herald/condolences-charities.aspx?keyword=coycada&amp;pid=166522666" target="_self"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><span style="
2 CONC font-size: small;">charity of your choice</span></span></a><span style="font-size: small;">. Online Obituary @ </span><a href="http://www.brunners.com/" target="_blank"><span style="font-size: small;"
2 CONC >www.brunners.com.</span></a></span></p> <p></div> </div> </div> <p style="text-align: left;" dir="ltr">&nbsp;</p></p>
