1 NOTE Funeral services for Dolores A. Cichon, 77, of Wickliffe, will be 11:30 a.m. Tuesday, April 6, 2010, at St. Mary Magdalene Church, 32114 Vine St., Willowick, OH 44095. <p></p> <p>Mrs. Cichon passed aw
2 CONC ay March 31, 2010, at Manor Care in Willoughby.</p> <p></p> <p>She was born Nov. 14, 1932, in Cleveland.</p> <p></p> <p>Mrs. Cichon was a retired electrical assembler from Picker International.</p> <p
2 CONC ></p> <p>Survivors are her daughters, Donna (Robert) Bezoski of Mentor and Cheryl (Barry) Lane of Madison; sons, Christopher (Diana) of Newbury and Donald of Wickliffe; grandchildren, Rachel Bezoski, 
2 CONC Matthew and Nicholas Cichon, Alexander and Kyle Cichon and Shelby Lane; sisters, Rose Grabitz, Lillian Rancourt and Louise (Frank) Marold; and brothers, Frank and Albert (Betty). <p></p> <p>She was pr
2 CONC eceded in death by her husband, Chester J.; daughter, Diane; sisters, Florence Conkling, Mary Ventresca, Angela Parise, Theresa Mandato, Josephine DiBartolomeo and Jennie McManney; and brothers, Antho
2 CONC ny, Michael and Joseph Mandato. <p></p> <p>Friends may call from 2 to 4 and 6 to 9 p.m. Monday at Vicchiarelli Funeral Home, 5252 Mayfield Road, Lyndhurst. Father Ted Lucas of St. Mary Magdalene in Wi
2 CONC llowick will officiate. Burial will be in All Souls Cemetery in Chardon Township.  <p></p> <p></p>
