2 NOTE Teresita Jane “Terry” Miller, age 77, of New Philadelphia, died peacefully, Wednesday, June 12, 2019, in the Inn at Northwood Village following a period of declining health.Born in the family home
3 CONC  at New Philadelphia on November 25, 1941, Terry was a daughter of the late Michael Seibold and Anna Cihon Fox.She graduated from St. Joseph at Dover and briefly worked in a doctor’s office prior to
3 CONC  starting her career in the banking industry. She started as a teller with the former Reeves Bank and ultimately retired as a Branch Manager from Huntington Bank.Terry was an active member of the Libr
3 CONC a-Cura Chapter of CCL, the LCBA, T-4-C, the Red Hat Society and a volunteer with Share-A-Christmas for many years. She enjoyed crafting projects, cross stitch, sewing, working in her flower gardens, r
3 CONC eading, collecting pig figurines and memorabilia, attending country music concerts with her family and was known for her quick wit and sense of humor.Terry will be missed by her children, Matthew (Kim
3 CONC  Smith) Miller of Canal Fulton and Kristin (Dean) McClune of Denver, Colorado, a step-granddaughter, Caley (Casey) Helget of Utah and her step-great-grandchildren, Harper and Waylen. Also surviving ar
3 CONC e her siblings, Antonia Conn, Barbara Young, Christine Stevenson, and William (Jill) Seibold; sisters-in-law, Jo Anne Seibold and Linda Miller all of New Philadelphia as well as numerous nieces and ne
3 CONC phews.In addition to her parents, Terry was preceded in death by a brother, Michael Seibold and two brothers-in-law, Tom Conn and Tommy Young.The family will greet guests on Friday, June 14, 2019, fro
3 CONC m 1-2 PM in the Linn-Hert-Geib Funeral Home & Crematory at New Philadelphia. Fr. Jeff Coning will lead a service celebrating Terry’s life in the funeral home’s chapel at 2 PM. Burial will follow i
3 CONC n Calvary Cemetery at New Philadelphia.Instead of floral contributions, the family requests memorial contributions in Terry’s name be directed to The Alzheimer’s Association 408 9th Street SW, Can
3 CONC ton, Ohio 44707, to The Parkinson’s Disease Association 710 W 168th Street, New York, New York 10032, or to T-4-C Share-A-Christmas, 1458 5th Street NW, New Philadelphia, Ohio 44663.
2 AGE 77
1 FAMC @F23@
