2 NOTE <p>Carmella Kornetti<br />Carmella Kornetti passed away Sunday<br />morning May 7th 2017. She was born<br />Carmella Catherine Pezzullo on July 22,<br />1939 to parents Antoinette and Vincent<br />Pez
3 CONC zullo of New York City. Carmella<br />obtained her nursing degree from<br />Helene Fuld School of Nursing, Trenton,<br />New Jersey in 1960. She married John<br />&ldquo;Jack&rdquo; Kornetti on Novemb
3 CONC er 10, 1962,<br />a resident of Marathon, Florida and<br />employed by Southern Bell Telephone<br />Company. Carmella was one of the first<br />registered nurses working general duty<br />and emergenc
3 CONC y services at Fisherman&rsquo;s<br />Community Hospital. Her employment<br />there continued intermittently from 1963<br />through 1978 at which time she became<br />the Public Health Nurse for Florid
3 CONC a<br />Department of Health in Marathon.<br />As a small clinic, she managed many<br />programs, her favorite being Maternal<br />Health and Healthy Start. Carmella was<br />instrumental in the birth 
3 CONC of many young<br />people living in Marathon today. She also<br />was active in health education at Stanley<br />Switlik Elementary and Marathon High<br />School. Carmella was a compassionate<br />nur
3 CONC se and genuine human being, well<br />thought of and respected by the clients<br />and families she served. She was<br />someone who always put the care of<br />children and those who were sick and<br
3 CONC  />injured first. She was well known for the<br />enduring loving kindness she had for<br />her family, friends, and patients. Carmella<br />had frequent knocks at her door at all<br />hours of the da
3 CONC y or night from anybody<br />who needed medical attention. She<br />and Jack raised four children, all born<br />and raised in Marathon and graduates<br />of Marathon High School. They were<br />looki
3 CONC ng forward to celebrate their 55th<br />wedding anniversary this year. Carmella<br />is survived by her husband J. A.<br />Kornetti; Daughters Veronica M. Lowry<br />husband Steve of Tampa Florida and
3 CONC <br />Stephanie A. Irvin, husband Brett, Sons<br />John V. Kornetti and Paul A Kornetti,<br />wife Aimee 11 grandchildren 1 great<br />granddaughter. Living members of<br />her immediate family are: S
3 CONC isters<br />Carrie DeMartino, Ann Denny, Victoria<br />Tate, Giulietta Passarelli &ldquo;sister of her<br />heart, Lyn Rabito Lenard and Brother<br />Vincent Pezzullo. The family asks that<br />in lie
3 CONC u of gifts or flowers, please make a<br />memorial donation in Carmella&rsquo;s name to<br />her favorite charity, St. Jude&rsquo;s Children&rsquo;s<br />Hospital. Masses in her honor will be<br />hel
3 CONC d at San Pablo Catholic Church on<br />the following dates<br />5/29 , 6/2 , 6/15 , 7/5 , 7/22 , 8AM.<br />7/16, 7/30 , 8/6 , 8/13 , 11AM<br />7/29 , 5PM</p>
