1 NOTE <p style="widows: 1; text-transform: none; background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; margin: 0px 0px 1.53em; font: 13px/19px Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif; white-space: normal; let
2 CONC ter-spacing: normal; color: #111111; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; padding: 0px;">Andrew S. Cihon, age 93, of Midvale, died Thursday, May 21, 2015 in Beacon Pointe Rehabilitation 
2 CONC Center at Uhrichsville following a period of declining health.&nbsp;A son of the late Max and Anna Cihon, Andy was born at Roswell, Ohio on November 28, 1921.</p> <p style="widows: 1; text-transform: 
2 CONC none; background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; margin: 0px 0px 1.53em; font: 13px/19px Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif; white-space: normal; letter-spacing: normal; color: #111111; 
2 CONC word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; padding: 0px;">He attended school at Roswell and in 1936, joined the Civilian Conservation Corps, Company 1586 in Bozeman, Montana. In 1942, Andy enl
2 CONC isted into the United States Army and served in the Asiatic Pacific Theatre during World War II and was discharged from active duty on December 3, 1945.</p> <p style="widows: 1; text-transform: none; 
2 CONC background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; margin: 0px 0px 1.53em; font: 13px/19px Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif; white-space: normal; letter-spacing: normal; color: #111111; word-s
2 CONC pacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; padding: 0px;">Upon returning to the Tuscarawas Valley he worked for a brief time for the former Joy Manufacturing at New Philadelphia before becoming empl
2 CONC oyed by then Warner &amp; Swasey in 1951. Following more than 30 years of service with the company as a lift truck driver and Parts Department laborer, Andy retired from the Gradall Company in 1982.</
2 CONC p> <p style="widows: 1; text-transform: none; background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; margin: 0px 0px 1.53em; font: 13px/19px Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif; white-space: normal; 
2 CONC letter-spacing: normal; color: #111111; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; padding: 0px;">Following his retirement, his greatest joy was time spent with family, especially his grandson
2 CONC s. He enjoyed fishing and hunting with his good friend and brother-in-law, Denton and was a Lifetime Member of the former Midvale VFW.</p> <p style="widows: 1; text-transform: none; background-color: 
2 CONC #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; margin: 0px 0px 1.53em; font: 13px/19px Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif; white-space: normal; letter-spacing: normal; color: #111111; word-spacing: 0px; -webk
2 CONC it-text-stroke-width: 0px; padding: 0px;">He is survived by three children, Diana (Jim) Sims of Midvale, David (Wendy) Cihon of New Philadelphia, and Brenda (Mike) Mitres of Tippecanoe; three grandson
2 CONC s, Adam Mackey, Blake (Brittany) Mackey, and Evan (Leslie) Cihon; a sister, Ann Fosnight, his brother-in-law, Denton Clagg and his sister-in-law, Theresa Cihon as well as numerous nieces and nephews.<
2 CONC /p> <p style="widows: 1; text-transform: none; background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; margin: 0px 0px 1.53em; font: 13px/19px Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif; white-space: normal;
2 CONC  letter-spacing: normal; color: #111111; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; padding: 0px;">In addition to his parents, Andy was preceded in death by his wife, Ruth, whom he married on 
2 CONC August 8, 1953 and celebrated 42 years of marriage prior to her passing on June 11, 1996; brothers, Joseph, John, Pete, and Mike Cihon and a sister, Mary Howard, and a granddaughter, Nicole Mackey.</p
2 CONC > <p style="widows: 1; text-transform: none; background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; margin: 0px 0px 1.53em; font: 13px/19px Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif; white-space: normal; l
2 CONC etter-spacing: normal; color: #111111; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; padding: 0px;">The family will greet guests one hour prior to services on Wednesday, May 27, 2015 from 9:00 &n
2 CONC dash; 10:00 AM in the Linn-Hert-Geib Funeral Home &amp; Crematory at New Philadelphia where Pastor Brian Flood will lead a service celebrating Andy&rsquo;s life at 10:00 AM in the funeral home&rsquo;s
2 CONC  chapel. Burial, with military honors, will follow in the East Avenue Cemetery at New Philadelphia.</p> <p style="widows: 1; text-transform: none; background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; margin: 
2 CONC 0px 0px 1.53em; font: 13px/19px Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif; white-space: normal; letter-spacing: normal; color: #111111; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; padding:
2 CONC  0px;">Those wishing to do so may send the family a personal condolence and light a candle in remembrance of Andy by visiting the funeral home&rsquo;s website at www.GeibCares.com.</p> <p style="text-
2 CONC align: left;" dir="ltr">&nbsp;</p>
