2 CONC dth: 0px;">HORSKY, Bertha M.</h1></p><p><h5 id="dspDetail_byLine" class="updated dtstamp" style="margin: 0px; color: #999999; text-transform: none; line-height: normal; text-indent: 0px; letter-spacin
2 CONC g: 1px; padding-bottom: 5px; font-family: Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 0.8em; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: #
2 CONC ffffff; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;" title="2009-10-12T00:00:00Z">October 12, 2009</h5></p><p><div class="padBtm txtSmaller" style="font: 0.85em/normal Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color
2 CONC : #333333; text-transform: none; text-indent: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; margin-bottom: 10px; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: #ffffff; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><spa
2 CONC n class="author source-org vcard"><span class="org fn">Times Leader</span></span></div></p><p><div id="dspDetail_linksTop" class="navPaginate" style="font: 0.9em/normal Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans
2 CONC -serif; text-align: right; color: #666666; text-transform: none; text-indent: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; padding-bottom: 10px; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: #ffffff; -web
2 CONC kit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">HORSKY, Bertha M., 90, of Dillonvale, Ohio, died Saturday, October 10, 2009 in Heartland Lansing.</div></p><p><p>&nbsp;</p></p><p><p>&nbsp;</p></p><p><p style="margin: 5px
2 CONC  5px 10px; line-height: 18px;">She was born in Dillonvale on February 13, 1919, a daughter of the late Joseph and Mary Poniezalek Miller.</p></p><p><p style="margin: 5px 5px 10px; line-height: 18px;">
2 CONC In addition to her parents, she was preceded in death by her husband, Edward Horsky; a daughter, Melanie Diggs; four brothers: Charles, Edward, Mitchell and Stanley Miller; and a sister, Ann Gaul.</p>
2 CONC </p><p><p style="margin: 5px 5px 10px; line-height: 18px;">Bertha is survived by a son, Michael Horsky and his wife, Gladys; a daughter, Andrea Flint and her husband, Barry, all of Rayland, Ohio; two 
2 CONC sisters: Helen Pensis of Dillonvale and Theresa Pensis of Brook Park, Ohio; a brother, Joseph Miller of Garfield Heights, Ohio; three grandchildren: Cale Sterling, Christian Sterling and his wife, Ang
2 CONC el; Marcie Lynn Palm and her husband, Jonathan; three step- great-grandchildren and numerous nieces and nephews.</p></p><p><p style="margin: 5px 5px 10px; line-height: 18px;">Friends will be received 
2 CONC Tuesday, 2-4 and 6-8 p.m. at the Wilson Funeral Home, 154 Second Street, Dillonvale,OH with a vigil service at 7:30 p.m.</p></p><p><p style="margin: 5px 5px 10px; line-height: 18px;">Mass of Christian
2 CONC  Burial will be celebrated Wednesday October 14, 2009, at 10 a.m., at St. Adalbert Catholic Church, Dillonvale, with Reverend Dale Tornes, officiating.</p></p><p><p style="margin: 5px 5px 10px; line-h
2 CONC eight: 18px;">Interment will follow at St. Adalbert Cemetery, Dillonvale.</p></p><p><p>&nbsp;</p></p><p><p>&nbsp;</p></p><p dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;</p>
